J.A.R.V.I.S. — TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION

1. Project Overview

J.A.R.V.I.S. is a personal AI assistant designed as a native Android application.

The project is inspired by the fictional assistant from Iron Man.

The goal is to create an intelligent, voice-controlled assistant capable of reasoning, remembering information, executing approved actions and proactively helping the user.

2. Target Platform

Primary platform: Android.

Application type: Native Android application.

The application should support compatible Android smartphones.

3. Technology Stack

Programming Language

Kotlin.

Development Environment

Android Studio.

User Interface

Jetpack Compose.

AI Integration

External AI models accessed through secure APIs.

The architecture should allow different AI providers and models to be integrated.

Speech Recognition

Android speech recognition services and compatible offline solutions.

Text-to-Speech

Android TTS and compatible external voice services.

Local Database

Room Database.

Networking

HTTPS-based communication with external services.

Background Operations

Android-supported background execution mechanisms.

4. Application Architecture

The application should use a modular architecture.

Main modules:

- UI Module.
- AI Core Module.
- Voice Module.
- Memory Module.
- Action Module.
- Offline Module.
- Notification Module.
- Security Module.
- Data Module.

Each module should have clearly defined responsibilities.

5. AI Architecture

The AI Core should act as the central intelligence coordinator.

It should:

- Process user requests.
- Understand conversation context.
- Retrieve relevant memories.
- Select an appropriate AI model.
- Generate responses.
- Determine whether an action is required.
- Request confirmation when necessary.

6. Online and Offline Architecture

The application should support hybrid operation.

Online processing:

- Advanced AI reasoning.
- Internet searches.
- External API integrations.
- Cloud-based services.

Offline processing:

- Local memory access.
- Basic commands.
- Local notes and tasks.
- Available offline speech services.
- Basic local AI processing where supported.

7. Performance Requirements

The application should:

- Launch efficiently.
- Avoid unnecessary background activity.
- Minimize battery consumption.
- Handle network failures.
- Avoid blocking the user interface.
- Manage memory usage responsibly.

8. Security Requirements

The application must:

- Protect personal information.
- Store sensitive data securely.
- Protect API credentials.
- Request permissions only when necessary.
- Require confirmation for sensitive actions.
- Respect Android security restrictions.

9. User Interface Requirements

The interface should follow the established J.A.R.V.I.S. visual identity.

Main elements:

- Dark futuristic background.
- Electric blue energy core.
- Animated interface elements.
- Voice interaction indicators.
- System status panel.
- Conversation interface.
- Settings screen.

10. Development Requirements

Development should follow an incremental approach.

Each module should be:

1. Designed.
2. Implemented.
3. Tested.
4. Integrated.
5. Documented.

The application should remain modular and maintainable.

11. Hardware Considerations

Development will initially target a laptop with:

- 16 GB RAM preferred.
- SSD storage.
- Modern multi-core processor.
- Android-compatible development environment.

The exact hardware requirements may change as the project develops.

12. Future Scalability

The architecture should allow:

- Additional AI providers.
- New Android integrations.
- Improved local AI models.
- Additional languages.
- Smart home integrations.
- New assistant capabilities.

13. Development Status

Status: Planning.

The technical architecture is documented but not yet implemented.
